    "synthesis": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "synthesis",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Research low-risk overhead in partition enumeration: replace repeated scans for the last partition and copies of its vectors with move-from-back/pop-back, preserving the existing LIFO order. If measurements justify a second experiment, replace the maps in is_cycle with initialized vectors while preserving its BFS and ascending-neighbor scan. Check exact output and benchmark each change independently.",
        "B": "Investigate replacing find_min_key's repeated full scan with an ordered frontier keyed by (key, vertex index). The loaded adjacency entries are 0/1, so preserve the current leftmost-index tie behavior and ensure disconnected graphs still return the same result. Benchmark against the scan; the prior vector<char>/reduction variants measured 0.005476–0.005517 seconds, so do not assume this change helps.",
        "C": "Build on the fastest measured candidate by comparing recursive mutable-state DFS with an iterative frame-stack backtrack, preserving neighbor order, leaf-only evaluation, first-success behavior, and strict best-color tie handling. Also measure generic serial/parallel cutoffs and scheduling policies suited to a four-core target; merge results in the original order. Do not tune to particular test inputs.",
        "G": "Treat the measured 0.005208-second C candidate as the current best starting point, not as a guarantee that its changes combine well with others. Integrate only compatible tree results, benchmark the complete integration, and retain it only if correctness holds and its measured time improves. Recheck the official cases and exact path/color output; the slower or overlapping candidates are not presumed additive.",
        "analysis": "The task is tropical path search, with output compared against the provided sequential implementation; preserve its observable path selection and formatting for every valid input. Baseline mean was 0.005705 seconds. The best supplied candidate was C at 0.005208 seconds (about 8.7% faster); A const-reference changes measured 0.005379 seconds, B's find-min change 0.005476 seconds, and C's task-per-root/neighbor variant 0.005599 seconds. These are short measurements over four correctness cases on a four-core ARM64 target, so gains are modest evidence, not a basis for assuming additive effects. Keep the source, oracle, tests, compiler, and budgets unchanged; do not specialize to test values or replace the computation with expected answers."
